***************************** T A L Y S **************************1225 1451  192
                                                                  1225 1451  193
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   1225 1451  194
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      1225 1451  195
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    1225 1451  196
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     1225 1451  197
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  1225 1451  198
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        1225 1451  199
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    1225 1451  200
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         1225 1451  201
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      1225 1451  202
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    1225 1451  203
stored in this data file:                                         1225 1451  204
                                                                  1225 1451  205
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   1225 1451  206
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     1225 1451  207
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 1225 1451  208
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   1225 1451  209
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                1225 1451  210
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   1225 1451  211
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    1225 1451  212
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        1225 1451  213
- Recoil data                                                     1225 1451  214
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           1225 1451  215
- Total particle energy spectra                                   1225 1451  216
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      1225 1451  217
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        1225 1451  218
- Residual production cross sections                              1225 1451  219
                                                                  1225 1451  220
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            1225 1451  221
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        1225 1451  222
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   1225 1451  223
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                1225 1451  224
                                                                  1225 1451  225
***************** F I L E   I N F O R M A T I O N ****************1225 1451  226
                                                                  1225 1451  227
##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    1225 1451  228
                                                                  1225 1451  229
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       1225 1451  230
                                                                  1225 1451  231
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          1225 1451  232
                                                                  1225 1451  233
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   1225 1451  234
                                                                  1225 1451  235
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 1225 1451  236
                                                                  1225 1451  237
Details about the origin of the resonance parameters for this     1225 1451  238
nuclide are given above in this description. In general, both a   1225 1451  239
Resolved and an Unresolved Resonance Range are given.             1225 1451  240
                                                                  1225 1451  241
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                1225 1451  242
                                                                  1225 1451  243
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       1225 1451  244
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  1225 1451  245
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   1225 1451  246
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  1225 1451  247
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  1225 1451  248
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 1225 1451  249
to the highest incident energy.                                   1225 1451  250
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:1225 1451  251
                                                                  1225 1451  252
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  1225 1451  253
                                                                  1225 1451  254
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range,    1225 1451  255
or partly reproduced using experimental data.                     1225 1451  256
                                                                  1225 1451  257
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     1225 1451  258
                                                                  1225 1451  259
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    1225 1451  260
total cross section.                                              1225 1451  261
                                                                  1225 1451  262
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            1225 1451  263
                                                                  1225 1451  264
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    1225 1451  265
                                                                  1225 1451  266
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        1225 1451  267
                                                                  1225 1451  268
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  1225 1451  269
                                                                  1225 1451  270
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           1225 1451  271
                                                                  1225 1451  272
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   1225 1451  273
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        1225 1451  274
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     1225 1451  275
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         1225 1451  276
sections.                                                         1225 1451  277
                                                                  1225 1451  278
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 1225 1451  279
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 1225 1451  280
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 1225 1451  281
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 1225 1451  282
- MT51-90  : (n,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      1225 1451  283
- MT91     : (n,n') continuum cross section                       1225 1451  284
- MT102    : (n,gamma) cross section                              1225 1451  285
- MT103    : (n,p) cross section                                  1225 1451  286
- MT104    : (n,d) cross section                                  1225 1451  287
- MT105    : (n,t) cross section                                  1225 1451  288
- MT106    : (n,h) cross section                                  1225 1451  289
- MT107    : (n,a) cross section                                  1225 1451  290
- MT600-610: (n,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       1225 1451  291
- MT649    : (n,p) continuum cross section                        1225 1451  292
- MT650-655: (n,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        1225 1451  293
- MT699    : (n,d) continuum cross section                        1225 1451  294
- MT700-705: (n,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        1225 1451  295
- MT749    : (n,t) continuum cross section                        1225 1451  296
- MT750-755: (n,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        1225 1451  297
- MT799    : (n,h) continuum cross section                        1225 1451  298
- MT800-810: (n,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       1225 1451  299
- MT849    : (n,a) continuum cross section                        1225 1451  300
                                                                  1225 1451  301
##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           1225 1451  302
                                                                  1225 1451  303
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    1225 1451  304
discrete levels.                                                  1225 1451  305
                                                                  1225 1451  306
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         1225 1451  307
                                                                  1225 1451  308
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  1225 1451  309
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   1225 1451  310
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      1225 1451  311
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  1225 1451  312
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      1225 1451  313
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         1225 1451  314
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   1225 1451  315
on an angular grid.                                               1225 1451  316
                                                                  1225 1451  317
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       1225 1451  318
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        1225 1451  319
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         1225 1451  320
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         1225 1451  321
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         1225 1451  322
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        1225 1451  323
                                                                  1225 1451  324
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     1225 1451  325
                                                                  1225 1451  326
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     1225 1451  327
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   1225 1451  328
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  1225 1451  329
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             1225 1451  330
All data are generated with TALYS.                                1225 1451  331
                                                                  1225 1451  332
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   1225 1451  333
                                                                  1225 1451  334
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      1225 1451  335
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   1225 1451  336
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   1225 1451  337
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are1225 1451  338
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   1225 1451  339
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  1225 1451  340
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              1225 1451  341
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 1225 1451  342
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  1225 1451  343
For each residual product:                                        1225 1451  344
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               1225 1451  345
- the recoil                                                      1225 1451  346
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         1225 1451  347
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     1225 1451  348
sections.                                                         1225 1451  349
                                                                  1225 1451  350
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     1225 1451  351
                                                                  1225 1451  352
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  1225 1451  353
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 1225 1451  354
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          1225 1451  355
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       1225 1451  356
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 1225 1451  357
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     1225 1451  358
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  1225 1451  359
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      1225 1451  360
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         1225 1451  361
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             1225 1451  362
                                                                  1225 1451  363
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   1225 1451  364
followed:                                                         1225 1451  365
                                                                  1225 1451  366
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         1225 1451  367
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         1225 1451  368
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         1225 1451  369
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     1225 1451  370
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     1225 1451  371
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     1225 1451  372
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     1225 1451  373
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     1225 1451  374
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     1225 1451  375
                                                                  1225 1451  376
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 1225 1451  377
                                                                  1225 1451  378
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    1225 1451  379
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          1225 1451  380
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     1225 1451  381
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          1225 1451  382
                                                                  1225 1451  383
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  1225 1451  384
                                                                  1225 1451  385
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     1225 1451  386
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    1225 1451  387
as isomer.                                                        1225 1451  388
                                                                  1225 1451  389
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 1225 1451  390
                                                                  1225 1451  391
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        1225 1451  392
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    1225 1451  393
as isomer.                                                        1225 1451  394
                                                                  1225 1451  395
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          1225 1451  396
                                                                  1225 1451  397
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:1225 1451  398
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   1225 1451  399
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   1225 1451  400
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   1225 1451  401
  given                                                           1225 1451  402
                                                                  1225 1451  403
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          1225 1451  404
                                                                  1225 1451  405
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  1225 1451  406
                                                                  1225 1451  407
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 1225 1451  408
                                                                  1225 1451  409
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         1225 1451  410
                                                                  1225 1451  411
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   1225 1451  412
                                                                  1225 1451  413
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        1225 1451  414
and more details are given above in this description. In most     1225 1451  415
versions of TENDL, this information is now stored in MF33.        1225 1451  416
                                                                  1225 1451  417
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 1225 1451  418
                                                                  1225 1451  419
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  1225 1451  420
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     1225 1451  421
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    1225 1451  422
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   1225 1451  423
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  1225 1451  424
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                1225 1451  425
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      1225 1451  426
   same reaction channel between different energies)              1225 1451  427
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      1225 1451  428
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               1225 1451  429
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      1225 1451  430
   different reaction channels for different energies)            1225 1451  431
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        1225 1451  432
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              1225 1451  433
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  1225 1451  434
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       1225 1451  435
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     1225 1451  436
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  1225 1451  437
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     1225 1451  438
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     1225 1451  439
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     1225 1451  440
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   1225 1451  441
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   1225 1451  442
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  1225 1451  443
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   1225 1451  444
                                                                  1225 1451  445
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  1225 1451  446
                                                                  1225 1451  447
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       1225 1451  448
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  1225 1451  449
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates       1225 1451  450
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   1225 1451  451
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         1225 1451  452
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  1225 1451  453
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      1225 1451  454
representation is used.                                           1225 1451  455
                                                                  1225 1451  456
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      1225 1451  457
                                                                  1225 1451  458
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  1225 1451  459
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             1225 1451  460
                                                                  1225 1451  461
